    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432\">PR #14432</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>wasmtime serve</code> answers 500 when a request has neither a URI authority nor a<br>\n<code>Host</code> header. The rejection happens before the guest runs, so the error now<br>\ncarries the status the client should see, and <code>serve</code> reads it back, defaulting<br>\nto 500. That gives the 400 RFC 9112 section 3.2 asks for, and it is not<br>\nversion-specific: an HTTP/1.0 request without <code>Host</code> gets the same 400.<br>\n<code>wasi:http/service</code> is untouched.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 627822984,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790695792
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432#issuecomment-5893410546\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432\">PR #14432</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Your three steps are merged, but they don't actually solve the problem: the p2 prepare error gets wrapped into a TrapOrPanicError before serve gets it, so ErrorResponse is only logged and we still return a 500.</p>\n<p>To get a 400, we should pass this error back through tx just like instantiation errors do. This touches 6 test cases, but leaves service completely unchanged.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 627823797,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790695968
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432#issuecomment-5893482071\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432\">PR #14432</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Done in fdf05d286b. Passing the error back through tx gives us the 400 now; my earlier comment was describing the code before this fix.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 627824951,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790696221
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao edited a <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432#issuecomment-5893482071\">comment</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14432\">PR #14432</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Done in fdf05d286b. Passing the error back through tx gives us the 400 now; </p>\n</blockquote>",
